# Infrastructure layer rules

These rules apply when editing files under `src/LoreWeave.Infrastructure/`.

- Repositories implement the Domain role interfaces and live in
  `Infrastructure/Repositories/<Entity>/` — one class per entity
  (`CharacterRepository`, `FactRepository`, `KnowRelationRepository`).
- Cypher queries are `const string` (or `StringBuilder` for dynamic queries),
  always **parameterized** with anonymous-object parameters. Never concatenate
  user input into Cypher.
- IDs are stored as their database string form via `.ToDatabaseId()`. Convert
  back with `.DatabaseIdToGuid()`.
- Result mapping uses extension methods under `Repositories/Extensions/`
  (e.g. `record.ToCharacter()`).
- `Neo4jTransactionFactory` implements the Domain `ITransactionFactory` and
  yields `Neo4jTransaction` wrappers. Repository methods take the Domain
  `ITransaction` and unwrap it with `transaction.AsNeo4jTransaction()`
  (`Infrastructure/Transactions/TransactionExtensions`). Never resolve
  `IDriver` or sessions directly in repositories.
- Register new repositories in `IoC/RegisterDatabase.cs`: one scoped concrete
  class, with each role interface forwarded to it.
- The Cypher `SET` for updates always increments version:
  `SET ch.Version = ch.Version + 1`.